{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "The new library functions (U2-U8) will be implemented as a standalone Go package within the Hyperledger Fabric codebase to avoid tight coupling with existing CLI tools.",
    "For U1, the transaction validation and chaincode execution logic will be modified to include data values alongside keys and versions in the readset, allowing peers to detect tampering during the validation phase.",
    "For U2, the necessary data structures from the `genesisconfig` package will be copied and adapted into the new package, avoiding direct dependencies on `viper` and `yaml` processing.",
    "For U3 and U4, cryptographic operations will use standard Go crypto libraries, accepting key material directly as function parameters rather than reading from configuration files.",
    "For U7, the ConfigUpdate calculation logic will be implemented by comparing the base and modified configurations and computing the delta, replicating the behavior of `configtxlator compute_update`."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has a strong understanding of Hyperledger Fabric internals, including protobuf definitions, MSP, and transaction flow.",
    "Access to the Hyperledger Fabric source code and development environment is readily available.",
    "Unit and integration testing environments are already set up and can be easily extended for the new features.",
    "The effort estimates do not include time for code review iterations or addressing review comments, only the initial development and testing."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements Analysis and Architecture Design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze user stories U1-U8, design the new library package structure, define interfaces, and plan the modifications to the Fabric core for readset validation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Tampered Readset Invalidation (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Modify chaincode execution to include values in the readset and update the transaction validation logic to compare values and invalidate transactions if tampering is detected.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement Channel Creation Transaction Library (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the CreateChannelTx function, copy and adapt necessary structures from genesisconfig, and ensure it generates a proto-encoded genesis block without network access or key material assumptions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement Detached Signature Generation (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function to sign a ChannelUpdate transaction and generate a detached signature using provided key material.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement Signed Channel Config Update Assembly (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function to take a ConfigUpdate transaction and a collection of detached signatures to create a complete, signed channel config update transaction.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement Unsigned Channel Update for Batch Size (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a library function to generate an unsigned channel update transaction that modifies the max_message_count batch size parameter.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement Organization ConfigGroup Generation (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a library function to generate a ConfigGroup representing an Organization, accepting necessary cryptographic material directly as input.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Implement ConfigUpdate Calculation (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a library function to calculate a ConfigUpdate message that updates a base config to a modified config, equivalent to configtxlator compute_update.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Implement Consortium Org Addition (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Implement a function to add an org definition to a named consortium in system channel configuration, generating an unsigned channel update transaction.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Testing and Integration",
      "activity_description": "Write and execute unit tests for all new functions and modifications, and perform integration testing to ensure compatibility with existing Fabric components.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Document the new library functions, their parameters, and the changes to the readset validation logic.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 240
  }
}
```

